    "diff_hunk": "@@ -0,0 +1,27 @@\n+=== Data Only Devices and Buses\n+\n+IOPMPs may only protect from data only device such as general DMA.\n+The IOPMP under the general DMA in <<IOPMP_SE_Example>> illustrates an example integration.\n+In this scenario, instruction permission checking is not required.\n+Therefore, all permission bits related to instruction fetch (`x` in `ENTRY_CFG`, and `SRCMD_X`/`SRCMD_XH` of <<#SPS_EXT,SPS extension>>) can be fixed to 0, or not implemented.\n+\n+For some small-scale systems which have a single RISC-V hart with PMP and data-only bus initiators,\n+or for some system bus that don't provide any instruction fetch hint,\n+the IOPMP can treat the instruction fetch accesses as data read accesses.\n+This simplifies both the system and IOPMP configuration by fixing all instruction fetch permission bits to 0, or making them unavailable.\n+The field `HWCFG3.xinr` indicates whether the IOPMP data read permission treats the instruction fetch accesses as data read accesses.\n+\n+[NOTE]\n+====\n+A system with a single RISC-V hart that includes PMP and only data-only bus initiators can enforce execution permission checking entirely within the hart using its PMP.",
    "path": "application_note/data_devices_buses.adoc",
